WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:14.963
eyes went wide as he stared at the hole in the fence.

2
00:00:16.565 --> 00:00:19.627
"You want us to crawl through that hole, Ivy?

3
00:00:20.768 --> 00:00:23.450
But what if the opossums attack us?"

4
00:00:24.812 --> 00:00:25.552
Glen laughed.

5
00:00:27.194 --> 00:00:29.856
"Opossums are the friendliest forest creatures there are.

6
00:00:30.688 --> 00:00:32.289
Well, unless you wake them up."

7
00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:35.091
Ivy peeked through the hole.

8
00:00:35.111 --> 00:00:37.313
"Guys, this is perfect!

9
00:00:38.013 --> 00:00:39.134
We can escape tonight.

10
00:00:41.155 --> 00:00:43.457
Let's meet an hour after the last bugle call."

11
00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.321
So that was the plan.

12
00:00:52.663 --> 00:00:53.844
Ivy could hardly wait.

13
00:00:56.625 --> 00:01:00.088
That night she lay in her bunk, listening to all the sounds.

14
00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.781
Willow and Clara had finally stopped talking.

15
00:01:04.941 --> 00:01:06.562
Penelope snored softly.

16
00:01:08.263 --> 00:01:10.684
When it was time, Ivy slipped out of bed.

17
00:01:14.405 --> 00:01:16.286
She slowly opened the screen door.

18
00:01:17.406 --> 00:01:20.148
It squeaked a little but not enough to wake up the others.

19
00:01:24.029 --> 00:01:26.510
Ivy sneaked through the dark night toward the square.

20
00:01:27.831 --> 00:01:30.872
Up ahead, she saw what looked like two shining eyes.

21
00:01:32.008 --> 00:01:33.489
"Psst! Glen?

22
00:01:34.189 --> 00:01:35.850
Ezra? Is that you?"

23
00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:38.652
"Ivy! Over here!"

24
00:01:39.052 --> 00:01:40.773
Glen said a little too loudly.

25
00:01:42.374 --> 00:01:44.895
The two shining eyes were coming from Ezra's face.

26
00:01:46.456 --> 00:01:47.717
"What are you wearing?"

27
00:01:48.317 --> 00:01:48.937
Ivy asked.

28
00:01:48.957 --> 00:01:53.720
"These are my homemade night vision goggles," Ezra said.

29
00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:57.522
"I glued two mini flashlights to my glasses."

30
00:01:57.542 --> 00:02:01.364
"Wow, that's pretty cool," Ivy said.

31
00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:03.921
"I mean, if they actually work."

32
00:02:05.523 --> 00:02:07.324
The kids started down the dark trail.

33
00:02:08.765 --> 00:02:11.588
Ezra crashed into Glen, almost knocking him down.

34
00:02:11.608 --> 00:02:14.050
"Hey, watch it!"

35
00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:15.091
Glen yelled.

36
00:02:15.111 --> 00:02:17.553
"Sorry," Ezra said.

37
00:02:17.573 --> 00:02:21.296
A few minutes later, Ezra stepped on Ivy's toes.

38
00:02:21.316 --> 00:02:26.460
"Ouch! Ezra, try not to be so clumsy," Ivy said.

39
00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:31.184
"Sorry! I glued the flashlights in front of my eyes.

40
00:02:31.976 --> 00:02:33.436
I can't see anything!"

41
00:02:34.977 --> 00:02:35.657
Ivy sighed.

42
00:02:35.677 --> 00:02:39.018
"Try pushing the glasses up on your forehead."

43
00:02:42.339 --> 00:02:44.940
They tiptoed through the woods behind boys' cabins.

44
00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.280
They could hear someone strumming a ukulele.

45
00:02:52.042 --> 00:02:53.782
Mango," Glen whispered.

46
00:02:53.802 --> 00:02:56.983
"He thinks ukulele music puts us to sleep."

47
00:02:57.003 --> 00:03:02.037
"That horrible noise would give me nightmares," Ivy said.

48
00:03:06.279 --> 00:03:09.782
Just then Ezra tripped over a rock and made a loud noise.

49
00:03:09.802 --> 00:03:12.363
"Who—who's there?"

50
00:03:12.784 --> 00:03:13.584
Mango cried.

51
00:03:14.265 --> 00:03:16.006
Ivy and the boys froze in place.

52
00:03:16.026 --> 00:03:19.388
"Hoo, hoo, hoo, hoo, hoo!"

53
00:03:19.969 --> 00:03:21.830
Glen called, imitating an owl.

54
00:03:23.271 --> 00:03:24.512
They heard Mango chuckle.

55
00:03:25.412 --> 00:03:27.353
He went back to playing his ukulele.

56
00:03:29.215 --> 00:03:30.776
Overhead the moon was shining.

57
00:03:32.072 --> 00:03:34.134
Its silver light reflected off the lake.

58
00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:37.576
A million stars winked like tiny lights.

59
00:03:37.596 --> 00:03:41.319
"I hope we don't step on a snake."

60
00:03:42.279 --> 00:03:45.221
Ezra moved his head around so the flashlights lit up the path.

61
00:03:45.241 --> 00:03:49.705
"Snakes like sunlight, Ezra," Glen said.

62
00:03:49.725 --> 00:03:53.227
"At night we're more likely to run into skunks.

63
00:03:53.928 --> 00:03:54.408
Or wolves."

64
00:03:54.428 --> 00:03:59.752
"W-wolves?" Ezra asked, his voice shaking.

65
00:04:02.328 --> 00:04:04.449
Ivy poked Glen in the ribs with her elbow.

66
00:04:04.469 --> 00:04:06.369
"You're not being helpful."

67
00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:10.330
They came to a fork in the path.

68
00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:13.991
Ivy turned right, and Glen turned left.

69
00:04:16.252 --> 00:04:18.893
Ezra stumbled off the path and fell into a bush.

70
00:04:18.913 --> 00:04:24.795
"The hole in the fence is this way," Ivy said.

71
00:04:25.935 --> 00:04:26.955
Glen pointed left.

72
00:04:27.756 --> 00:04:29.016
"No, it's this way."

73
00:04:30.608 --> 00:04:32.269
"I think Ivy's right.

74
00:04:32.969 --> 00:04:34.029
I mean, correct.

75
00:04:34.789 --> 00:04:38.370
We go to the right," Ezra said, picking leaves out of his hair.

76
00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:40.411
Glen sighed.

77
00:04:40.431 --> 00:04:43.752
"We can't get lost.

78
00:04:44.152 --> 00:04:49.173
Then the amazing Glen Brown escape legend won't be very um, amazing."

79
00:04:50.593 --> 00:04:53.274
They hiked down the trail until Ivy stopped suddenly.

80
00:04:53.294 --> 00:04:56.495
"Look! There's the hole in the fence."

81
00:04:58.195 --> 00:05:00.056
She ducked down and crawled through the opening.

82
00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.281
Glen was right behind her.

83
00:05:03.742 --> 00:05:05.423
Ezra put one foot through the hole.

84
00:05:06.224 --> 00:05:08.685
Just then a shrill whistle pierced the night.

85
00:05:09.926 --> 00:05:12.168
A bright light shone right in the kids' eyes.

86
00:05:12.188 --> 00:05:14.249
"Freeze, campers!"

87
00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:15.530
a voice shouted.

88
00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:17.912
"Don't take another step!"
